# A session asks a question while the user is away. The phone gets the question with
# its choices numbered and how to answer. A reply is played into Copilot's form as
# keys, and the phone is told what Copilot recorded, because that record is the only
# account of what the form took. Nothing is "queued until this turn ends": the turn
# cannot end until the question is answered, so that would never come.

size 110x30
arg --mux
fake_telegram private
session existing-app Existing app session

wait_for Existing app session
press enter
wait_for Fake Copilot is idling

type e2e:ask 1500 Which colour should the header be? | Red | Green | Blue
press enter
press ctrl+b d
wait_for Existing app session

telegram_wait Question waiting for your response
telegram_wait Question: Which colour should the header be?
telegram_wait <b>Your answer</b>
telegram_wait 1. Red
telegram_wait 3. Blue
telegram_wait Reply with a number, or type another answer.
telegram_dump 01-question
dump 01-list-with-question

# A number picks that choice; the stub plays the form and records the answer.
telegram_say 3
wait 6000
telegram_wait took the answer: User responded: Blue
telegram_wait reaction on
telegram_expect_not Queued
telegram_expect_not Not delivered
telegram_dump 02-answered
press enter
wait_for Fake Copilot answered: Blue
dump 02-form-answered

# Text that is no choice goes through the Other row.
type e2e:ask 1500 Which font? | Serif | Sans
press enter
press ctrl+b d
wait_for Existing app session
telegram_wait Which font?
telegram_say Comic Sans, obviously
wait 6000
telegram_wait took the answer: User responded: Comic Sans, obviously
telegram_dump 03-other-answered
press enter
wait_for Fake Copilot answered: Comic Sans, obviously

# With the question answered, an ordinary reply goes into the composer as before.
press ctrl+b d
wait_for Existing app session
telegram_say Thanks, now write the footer
wait 4000
press enter
wait_for Fake Copilot received: Thanks, now write the footer
telegram_dump 04-after-answer
dump 04-reply-delivered
